// The header: the comment that says what the table is and how to read it.
//
// The metrics are printed from the font rather than written into the text, so
// the comment and txt_st can never disagree with the rows under them.

mkf_head(string[] strs, string path, int[] psh) {
  push(strs, (import mkf_head1) + path + (import mkf_head2));
  mkf_face(strs, psh);
  mkf_st(strs, psh);
} return void;
